            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Which of the following is not a quadrilateral? A. Square B. Triangle C. Rectangle D. Rhombus</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake</span>
                    <span >A triangle is also a type of quadrilateral.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-right">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Approach</span>
                    <span >A triangle only has 3 sides, so it is not a quadrilateral! A quadrilateral must have 4 sides.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-note">💡 Count the number of sides carefully! Quadrilateral = 4 sides.</div>
            </div>
        </div>
<div class="lf-trap-card" data-trap="T2" data-hq-id="LF-T2-AUTO">
            <div class="lf-trap-header">
                <span class="lf-trap-badge">T2</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-diff">⭐⭐</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-id">LF-T2-AUTO</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A shape has 4 sides, and each side is the same length. Is it a square?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake</span>
                    <span >4 equal sides = square.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-right">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Approach</span>
                    <span >Not necessarily! A rhombus also has 4 equal sides. A square also requires all 4 angles to be right angles (90°).</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-note">💡 Square = 4 equal sides + 4 right angles. Neither can be missing!</div>
            </div>
        </div>
